You can combine multiple interpolations within a single path segment using piecewise:

PATH.setHeadingInterpolation(
    HeadingInterpolator.piecewise(
        new PiecewiseNode(0, 0.3, HeadingInterpolator.linear(0, Math.toRadians(180))),
        new PiecewiseNode(0.3, 1, HeadingInterpolator.tangent)
    )
);

This turns 180° in the first 30% of the path, then follows the curve tangentially for the rest. Piecewise is useful when you need different behaviors at different stages of one segment.
